{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `6070539a`: a historical row waits in the same arm, and\nthe arm names which of two facts holds.\n\nI wrote in `e19f27b5` that I accept no second exception. This row\nchanges that sentence, and I say so. It is still one arm. A row\nthat the member typed under an earlier descriptor is the member's\nintention, and each release of an application can make such rows.\nA read that fails on one, or a view that hides one, is worse than\none more value of a closed field.\n\n1. One historical row never fails the read. The other rows of the\n   batch project as they do today.\n2. The store keeps the row, as the existing owner says. No read\n   and no step rewrites it or promotes it.\n3. The arm of `e19f27b5` gains one closed field with two values.\n   One value says that a record that is no request holds the key.\n   The other says that the row has another descriptor. You name\n   the field and the values.\n4. A row with another descriptor carries its key and its stored\n   descriptor digest. It carries no values: the client has not\n   refined them, and the client gives a page no content that it\n   has not checked.\n5. `dismiss(key)` removes the row. `restore(key)` stops with\n   `descriptor-mismatch` and changes nothing. Promotion of old\n   values into a new descriptor is no part of C4.\n6. A key with an ordinary custody record keeps its C3 entry, and\n   the historical row adds no values to that entry. When both\n   facts of item 3 hold for one key, the descriptor fact is the\n   one that the arm names. Each key still appears one time.\n7. One case in the `scope-client.test.ts` owner: a batch with one\n   current row and one historical row. The current row projects,\n   the historical row appears one time in the arm, `restore`\n   stops, and `dismiss` removes that row only.\n\nOne fact that I need in the implementation note, because it sets\nhow often a member meets item 4: which changes of an application\nor of the client change the descriptor digest that C4 receives. If\nan ordinary release changes it for a scope whose acts did not\nchange, tell me before C4 is compiled. That would make a lost form\nthe common case, and it needs its own request.\n\nStop and ask at a third kind of row.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}